<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title>CSS3 Responsive Page</title>

    <!-- Google Font -->
    <link href="https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Poppins:wght@300;500;700&display=swap" rel="stylesheet">

    <!-- Font Awesome Icons -->
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.0/css/all.min.css">

    <style>
        * {
            margin: 0;
            padding: 0;
            box-sizing: border-box;
            font-family: 'Poppins', sans-serif;
        }

        body {
            background: #f4f4f4;
        }

        header {
            background: linear-gradient(45deg, #4facfe, #00f2fe);
            color: white;
            padding: 20px;
            text-align: center;
            animation: fadeIn 2s ease-in;
        }

        nav {
            display: flex;
            justify-content: center;
            background: #333;
        }

        nav a {
            color: white;
            padding: 14px 20px;
            text-decoration: none;
            transition: 0.3s;
        }

        nav a:hover {
            background: #4facfe;
            transform: scale(1.1);
        }

        .container {
            display: flex;
            flex-wrap: wrap;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .main {
            flex: 3;
            padding: 20px;
        }

        .sidebar {
            flex: 1;
            background: white;
            padding: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
        }

        /* Multi-column text */
        .columns {
            column-count: 3;
            column-gap: 20px;
        }

        .card {
            background: white;
            padding: 20px;
            margin-bottom: 20px;
            border-radius: 10px;
            transition: transform 0.4s;
        }

        .card:hover {
            transform: rotate(2deg) scale(1.03);
        }

        .icon {
            font-size: 30px;
            color: #4facfe;
            margin-bottom: 10px;
        }

        footer {
            text-align: center;
            padding: 15px;
            background: #333;
            color: white;
        }

        /* Animation */
        @keyframes fadeIn {
            from {
                opacity: 0;
                transform: translateY(-20px);
            }
            to {
                opacity: 1;
                transform: translateY(0);
            }
        }

        /* Responsive */
        @media (max-width: 768px) {
            .columns {
                column-count: 1;
            }

            .container {
                flex-direction: column;
            }
        }
    </style>
</head>
<body>

<header>
    <h1>My Responsive CSS3 Page</h1>
    <p>Using Animations, Columns, Icons & More</p>
</header>

<nav>
    <a href="#">Home</a>
    <a href="#">About</a>
    <a href="#">Services</a>
    <a href="#">Contact</a>
</nav>

<div class="container">

    <div class="main">

        <div class="card">
            <i class="fas fa-laptop-code icon"></i>
            <h2>Web Development</h2>
            <p class="columns">
                Web development is the process of creating, building, and maintaining websites and web applications
                for the internet or intranet. It involves coding (HTML, CSS, JavaScript) to ensure functionality 
                and user interaction, ranging from simple static pages to complex, dynamic web applications, 
                often categorized into front-end (client-side) and back-end (server-side) development. 

            </p>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
            <i class="fas fa-mobile-alt icon"></i>
            <h2>Responsive Design</h2>
            <p class="columns">
                Responsive design is a web development approach that ensures websites automatically adapt,
                resize, and rearrange content to provide optimal viewing and interaction across various devices, 
                from desktop monitors to mobile phones. It uses fluid grids, flexible images, and CSS3 media queries 
                to create a single, consistent, user-friendly experience rather than separate sites. 

            </p>
        </div>

    </div>

    <aside class="sidebar">
        <h3><i class="fas fa-info-circle"></i> Info</h3>
        <p>This sidebar includes icons and clean styling.</p>
    </aside>

</div>

<footer>
    <p>© 2026 My Website</p>
</footer>

</body>
</html>
